# Document review

- Read AGENTS.md and SRS.md before changing behavior.
- SRS.md is the functional spec. Update it in the same change when behavior changes.
- Postgres is written before a BullMQ job is enqueued. Redis is only the queue.
- Corrections are review rows. Do not overwrite extracted values.
- Evidence that cannot be located in that version's parsed text is a gap.
- Empty parsed text fails the version. Do not invent a page of gaps.
- Approve is rejected on gaps. Correct is allowed.
- Enqueue deletes any existing `extract-{versionId}` job, then adds it. Waiting on a previous version delays that same job.
- No code comments. Imports stay at the top of the file.
- Switch on unions and enums exhaustively, with a `never` default.
- Do not add auth, quote highlighting, or a live deploy.
- Keep the Postgres and Redis memory caps in docker-compose.yml.
